    {
      "label": null,
      "text": "The two editors have no common 'first frame' event: rustode's is the return from its first wgpu present, the App's closest events are Chromium's first contentful paint and the first fixture line seen in the DOM (polled over CDP). The comparison is therefore approximate: read the rustode number against the interval between the App's two, and do not divide one by the other. When the App launches were traced (rows 'launch to first swap' and 'launch to second swap'), the first swap is the closest counterpart of rustode's first frame: the display compositor's first drawn-and-swapped frame after the first line entered the DOM (gaps.md G22); say which event a ratio uses, and that the swap may be one frame early (the second swap bounds it). Both editors ran on the same virtual display with software rendering, with the same fixture on their command line."
    }
